Expanded story:
Amy stirred a pot of oatmeal on the stove while Will and Amber giggled at their cereal bowls. The kitchen hummed with normal morning chatter until a groaning shudder cracked through the front door—an undead creature burst in, its eyes glazed, arms reaching for her kids.

Quick as a heartbeat, Amy scooped Will into one arm and pressed Amber against her chest, sprinting toward the back closet that served as their safe spot. She shoved them inside, slammed the door, and turned to face the chaos. The zombie’s groan echoed through the hallway as she ran back to the kitchen.

She slipped under a loose floorboard in the pantry, pulled out a pistol tucked behind a stack of canned beans, then slid a gleaming katana from its sheath on the counter. With both weapons ready, Amy faced the first zombie that lunged at her—she fired a single shot, sending it sprawling into the kitchen tiles.

A second creature surged forward; she swung the katana in a swift arc, severing its neck with a clean slice. The third zombie staggered from the hallway, eyes wide as it tried to grasp her again. Amy spun, firing another round that sent it crashing against the fridge.

The last of the zombies thudded to the floor, dead. Breathing hard, she grabbed Will and Amber’s hands once more and hurried back through the closet door into the kitchen. The two kids clung to her as she pushed them out of the house—safe at last.
